1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,160
Sworn is for Tempo Zones: private ledgers on Tempo.

2
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:10,240
You'll see a real Zone proof, our own Zone settling only after it,

3
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:14,450
and a forged batch rejected — all real testnet transactions.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,753
This is Sworn's local console.

5
00:00:16,803 --> 00:00:25,042
The operator picks a Zone batch, here one withdrawal and two user transactions, and starts a proof job:

6
00:00:25,092 --> 00:00:31,950
Tempo's own code runs in a zero-knowledge VM, and the result goes to an auditor.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,969
A ZonePortal queues a batch's withdrawals only after its verifier accepts the batch,

8
00:00:38,019 --> 00:00:40,746
so that check must be trusted.

9
00:00:40,796 --> 00:00:44,450
In our own Zone, the verifier is Sworn.

10
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,795
The witness stays with the operator and the prover.

11
00:00:48,845 --> 00:00:52,657
Only hashes, counters and batch metadata reach Tempo:

12
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:58,450
enough to check the proof, not to see balances, senders or amounts.

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,950
The evidence panel reads Moderato live.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:13,450
Its pre-T13 prototype verifier accepts a malformed batch; Sworn demonstrates the missing ZK check.

15
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:23,489
Now Sworn, on a real batch from Tempo's integration tests: two user transactions and one withdrawal.

16
00:01:23,539 --> 00:01:32,901
Tempo's own batch verifier ran inside a zero-knowledge VM, and this contract checked the proof.

17
00:01:32,951 --> 00:01:36,666
Here it is on the explorer.

18
00:01:36,716 --> 00:01:40,430
Again, live: the real batch, true.

19
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:45,450
Change one field, and it reverts: invalid proof.

20
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,241
Now our own Zone on Moderato.

21
00:01:48,291 --> 00:01:52,892
Its portal called the verifier in each of three batches.

22
00:01:52,942 --> 00:02:00,334
Only after the last proof passed could this withdrawal be paid: our sequencer then called processWithdrawals.

23
00:02:00,384 --> 00:02:05,450
Here is the payout on the explorer: zero point five pathUSD.

24
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,709
Our sequencer submitted a forged batch: valid signature, made-up withdrawal queue, replayed proof.

25
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:13,635
The portal rejected it.

26
00:02:13,685 --> 00:02:18,450
No batch settled, and the Zone state did not change.

27
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:23,492
To be clear: the batch above comes from a dev chain.

28
00:02:23,542 --> 00:02:28,075
The Zone that paid is our own Zone on Moderato,

29
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:31,283
run by us, not a Tempo-created Zone.

30
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:34,950
Tempo's own Zones still use their current verifier.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,064
Sworn has no customers, revenue or payer agreement today.

32
00:02:39,114 --> 00:02:43,636
The next test is one Zone business supplying a batch;

33
00:02:43,686 --> 00:02:50,950
its reviewer re-verifies it and decides whether the next batch or upgrade is worth paying for.
